kind how-do-i
title How do I try a font set whose font file is installed but not active?
intro vtium draws only the font files that batch.conf lists as active, and treats every other font file as missing. vtium-config says when a font set's file is not active, and offers to activate it.
see fonts/use-a-font-file-that-is-not-active
waits-for CF1 item 3 and item 4: a trial offers font sets whose fonts vtium refuses, and nothing says why the built-in font draws

# wide.bdf is installed, but batch.conf lists only mono.bdf, so vtium
# treats wide.bdf as missing.
file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = mono
    [head console]
    vt = 5
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
font fonts/wide.bdf 10x20
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
frit wide
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/wide.bdf

at the start
check console draws mono

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Highlight wide.
at wide is highlighted
check screen shows "not among the active fonts"

3. Press t to try live.
at the trial
check console fell-back no
check screen shows "active"
